Final end-to-end results, i4i.metal with the cache on instance NVMe.

date_utc: 2026-07-27

Acceptance, vhost-user, local file object store:

  metal e2e: 23 passed, 0 failed

First fully green acceptance run. The one check that had failed on every previous
run -- "guest includes apt, curl and git" -- was broken, not the image: it asked
dash for three tools in a single `command -v`, which resolves only the first
operand. See metal-rebench.log for the earlier 22/1 runs.

10 concurrent cold creates, vhost-user, real S3:

  vhost-user-s3,create,10,10,...   batch wall 8146 ms, settled at 8173 ms, 0 failures

Compare with the same test earlier in the day:

  copy the rootfs, serial reconcile        121448 ms   4 failed
  golden root, serial reconcile             61637 ms   0 failed
  golden root, concurrent reconcile          8328 ms   0 failed  (local file store)
  golden root, concurrent reconcile          8146 ms   0 failed  (real S3)

The object store no longer affects concurrent create at all -- 8146 ms on S3
against 8328 ms on a local store -- because golden roots mean a create uploads no
data. Before, the same test was 121 s and lost four of ten.
